  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian NGO Cooperation Program (ANCP) accreditation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funding to support the Accreditation and assurance processes for Australian NGOs as part of the Australian NGO Cooperation Program (ANCP). Accreditation of Australian NGOs (ANGOs) is a front-end and rigorous risk-management process, which is also a robust due diligence process for DFAT. To receive funding under the ANCP, ANGOs must be accredited by DFAT. To gain accreditation Australian NGOs undergo a thorough and independent assessment of their organisational policies, systems and practices against an agreed set of accreditation criteria. Accreditation can also be used as a prerequisite for other NGO funding streams within DFAT. The assurance activities assess and monitor compliance with the ANCP Annual Grant Agreement. The ANCP has contributed to sustainable economic growth and poverty reduction in some of the world&apos;s poorest countries.</narrative>
  </description>
